    kg:textSpan "for establishing correspondence between specic object parts in dierent images (e.g. faces have a particular spatial conguration of the eyes and nose). However, an intriguing possibility is that deep models might be implicitly computing them. To explore this, we take 5 randomly drawn dog images with frontal pose and systematically mask out the same part of the face in each image (e.g. all left eyes, see Fig. 8 ). For each image i , we then compute: l i = x l i x l i , where x l i and x l i are th" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1311_2901_rag__chunk_010> a kg:Chunk ;
