    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/1412_3555_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "memory content is c j t = tanh ( W c x t + U c h t 1 ) j . The extent to which the existing memory is forgotten is modulated by a forget gate f j t , and the degree to which the new memory content is added to the memory cell is modulated by an input gate i j t . Gates are computed by f j t = ( W f x t + U f h t 1 + V f c t 1 ) j , i j t = ( W i x t + U i h t 1 + V i c t 1 ) j . Note that V f and V i are diagonal matrices. 3 Unlike to the traditional recurrent unit which overwrites its content at" .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1412_3555_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
