    kg:textSpan "2 memory vector c l t . At each time step the LSTM can choose to read from, write to, or reset the cell using explicit gating mechanisms. The precise form of the update is as follows: sigm sigm sigm tanh i f o g c l t = f c l t 1 + i g W l h l 1 t h l t 1 = h l t = o tanh( c l t ) Here, the sigmoid function sigm and tanh are applied element-wise, and W l is a [ 4 n 2 n ] matrix. The three vectors i, f, o R n are thought of as binary gates that control whether each memory cell is updated, whether" .

