    kg:textSpan "language separately, using images and sentences from separate training sets. Some work on attention mechanisms also uses merge architectures with at- 8 tention mechanisms by merging a dierent image representation at every time step. You et al. (2016) and Xu et al. (2015) merge as well as par-inject the attended visual regions, whilst Lu et al. (2016) only merge the regions whilst par-injecting a xed image representation. Though they do not use an RNN and hence are not focussed on in this review," .

