    kg:textSpan "can be viewed as the concept of low variation in the parameter space ; i.e., a small perturbation in the parameter space around a solution results in a small change in the loss surface. Several studies have provided arguments for generalization in deep learning based on flat minima (Keskar et al., 2017). However, Dinh et al. (2017) showed that flat minima in practical deep learning hypothesis spaces can be turned into sharp minima via re-parameterization without affecting the generalization gap," .

