    kg:textSpan "ImageNet). Intuitively, whereas statistical learning theory considers a set P D because of weak assumptions, some empirical studies can focus on a specified point ( P ( X,Y ) , S ) in a set P D because of stronger assumptions. Therefore, by using the same terminology such as expected risk and generalization in both cases, we are susceptible to confusion and apparent contradiction. Lower bounds, necessary conditions and tightness in statistical learning theory are typically defined via a worst-ca" .

