    kg:textSpan "deleted if n > q , otherwise q n zero rows are added. The aforementioned pooling methods mainly consider graph features and ignore the structural information of graphs. Recently, a differentiable pooling (DiffPool) [ 54 ] is proposed, which can generate hierarchical representations of graphs. Compared to all previous coarsening methods, DiffPool does not simply cluster the nodes in a graph but learns a cluster assignment matrix S at layer k referred to as S ( k ) R n k n k +1 , where n k is the " .

