    kg:textSpan "node assignments which consider both topological and feature information of a graph, so Equation 28 can be implemented with any standard ConvGNNs. However, the drawback of DiffPool is that it generates dense graphs after pooling and thereafter the computational complexity becomes O ( n 2 ) . Most recently, the SAGPool [ 102 ] approach is proposed, which considers both node features and graph topology and learns the pooling in a self-attention manner. Overall, pooling is an essential operation to" .

