    kg:textSpan "ne-tuning. The optimal adapter size varies per dataset. For example, 256 is chosen for MNLI, whereas for the smallest dataset, RTE, 8 is chosen. Restricting always to size 64 , leads to a small decrease in average accuracy to 79 . 6 . To solve all of the datasets in Table 1 , ne-tuning requires 9 the total number of BERT parameters. 4 In contrast, adapters require only 1 . 3 parameters. columns: col1 | col2 | col3 | col4 | col5 | col6 | col7 | col8 | col9 | col10 | col11 | col12 row: col1=The nu" .

