    kg:textSpan "other weight compression techniques must be used to attain further savings. Our bottleneck adapters can be much smaller, and still perform well. Multi-task Learning Multi-task learning (MTL) involves training on tasks simultaneously. Early work shows that sharing network parameters across tasks exploits task regularities, yielding improved performance ( Caruana , 1997 ). The authors share weights in lower layers of a network, and use specialized higher layers. Many NLP systems have exploited MTL" .

