    kg:textSpan ") denote the vector of inputs into layer l , y ( l ) denote the vector of outputs from layer l ( y (0) = x is the input). W ( l ) and b ( l ) are the weights and biases at layer l . The feed-forward operation of a standard neural network (Figure 3a) can be described as (for l { 0 , . . . , L 1 } and any hidden unit i ) where f is any activation function, for example, f ( x ) = 1 / (1 + exp( x )). With dropout, the feed-forward operation becomes (Figure 3b) r ( l ) j Bernoulli( p ) , e y ( l ) = " .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/JMLRdropout_rag__chunk_021> a kg:Chunk ;
