    kg:textSpan "of interest into a small feature map with a xed spatial extent of H W ( e.g ., 7 7 ), where H and W are layer hyper-parameters that are independent of any particular RoI. In this paper, an RoI is a rectangular window into a conv feature map. Each RoI is dened by a four-tuple ( r, c, h, w ) that species its top-left corner ( r, c ) and its height and width ( h, w ) . bounding box and hence L loc is ignored. For bounding-box regression, we use the loss stems from the fact that each RoI may have a " .

<http://example.org/kg/chunk/1504_08083_rag__chunk_004> a kg:Chunk ;
