    kg:textSpan "ENGIO We begin, in Section 3, by illustrating that, even in the case of linear models, hypothesis spaces with overwhelming capacity can result in arbitrarily small test errors and expected risks. Here, test error is the error of a learned hypothesis on data that it was not trained on, but which is often drawn from the same distribution. Test error is a measure of how well the hypothesis generalizes to new data. We closely examine this phenomenon, extending the original open problem from previous" .

