    kg:docId "JMLRdropout_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/JMLRdropout_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "and the units are not allowed to build co-adaptations freely. Therefore, if an n -sized layer is optimal for a standard neural net on any given task, a good dropout net should have at least n/p units. We found this to be a useful heuristic for setting the number of hidden units in both convolutional and fully connected networks. 1952 Dropout A.2 Learning Rate and Momentum Dropout introduces a signicant amount of noise in the gradients compared to standard stochastic gradient descent. Therefore, " .

