    kg:textSpan "baselines (55.3% to 63.9%), but only a surprisingly modest improvement compared to single-frame models (59.3% to 60.9%). We further study the generalization performance of our best model by retraining the top layers on the UCF- 101 Action Recognition dataset and observe signicant performance improvements compared to the UCF-101 baseline model (63.3% up from 43.9%). 1. Introduction Images and videos have become ubiquitous on the internet, which has encouraged the development of algorithms that ca" .

