    kg:docId "jozefowicz15_rag" ;
    kg:inPaper <http://example.org/kg/paper/jozefowicz15_rag> ;
    kg:textSpan "cell. we can close the gap between the LSTM and the better architectures. Thus, we recommend to increase the bias to the forget gate before attempting to use more sophisticated approaches. We also performed ablative experiments to measure the importance of each of the LSTMs many components. We discovered that the input gate is important, that the output gate is unimportant, and that the forget gate is extremely significant on all problems except language modelling. This is consistent with Mikolo" .

