    :hasEvidenceText "BN transform is a differentiable transformation that introduces normalized activations into the network."^^xsd:string,
        "Batch Normalization We have presented a novel mechanism for dramatically accelerating the training of deep networks."^^xsd:string,
        "Batch Normalization makes the distribution more stable and reduces the internal covariate shift."^^xsd:string,
        "Batch Normalization: Accelerating Deep Network Training by Reducing Internal Covariate Shift"^^xsd:string,
        "These plain networks are trained with BN [16], which ensures forward propagated signals to have non-zero variances."^^xsd:string,
        "batch normalization regularizes the model and reduces the need for Dropout (Srivastava et al., 2014). Finally, Batch Normalization makes it possible to use saturating nonlinearities"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :entity,
        owl:Thing ;
    skos:altLabel "BatchNormalization"^^xsd:string ;
    skos:skos_definition "A normalization technique that regularizes the model, reduces the need for Dropout, and prevents networks from getting stuck in saturated modes."^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom "CQ_S0_R1_0044"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0052"^^xsd:string,
        "CQ_S0_R1_0085"^^xsd:string,
