    kg:textSpan "generative adversarial networks (GAN) [ 110 ]. A GAN plays a competition game between a generator and a discriminator in training generative models. A generator tries to generate fake samples to be as real as possible while a discriminator attempts to distinguish the fake samples from real ones. Inspired by GANs, ARVGA endeavors to learn an encoder that produces an empirical distribution q ( Z | X , A ) which is indistinguishable from the prior distribution p ( Z ) . Similar as GAE*, GraphSage [" .

